#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-upload-pack.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "git-upload-pack(1)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-upload-pack.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-upload-pack.adoc:7
msgid "git-upload-pack - Send objects packed back to git-fetch-pack"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-upload-pack.adoc:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-upload-pack.adoc:14
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t'git-upload-pack' [--[no-]strict] [--timeout=<n>] [--stateless-rpc]\n"
"\t\t\t  [--advertise-refs] <directory>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-upload-pack.adoc:16
#, no-wrap
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-upload-pack.adoc:19
msgid ""
"Invoked by 'git fetch-pack', learns what objects the other side is missing, "
"and sends them after packing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-upload-pack.adoc:24
msgid ""
"This command is usually not invoked directly by the end user.  The UI for "
"the protocol is on the 'git fetch-pack' side, and the program pair is meant "
"to be used to pull updates from a remote repository.  For push operations, "
"see 'git send-pack'."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-upload-pack.adoc:26
#, no-wrap
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-upload-pack.adoc:28
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--strict`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-upload-pack.adoc:29
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-strict`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-upload-pack.adoc:31
msgid "Do not try <directory>/.git/ if <directory> is not a Git directory."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-upload-pack.adoc:32
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--timeout=<n>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-upload-pack.adoc:34
msgid "Interrupt transfer after <n> seconds of inactivity."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-upload-pack.adoc:35
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--stateless-rpc`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-upload-pack.adoc:39
msgid ""
"Perform only a single read-write cycle with stdin and stdout.  This fits "
"with the HTTP POST request processing model where a program may read the "
"request, write a response, and must exit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-upload-pack.adoc:40
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--http-backend-info-refs`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-upload-pack.adoc:47
msgid ""
"Used by linkgit:git-http-backend[1] to serve up "
"`$GIT_URL/info/refs?service=git-upload-pack` requests. See \"Smart Clients\" "
"in linkgit:gitprotocol-http[5] and \"HTTP Transport\" in the "
"linkgit:gitprotocol-v2[5] documentation. Also understood by "
"linkgit:git-receive-pack[1]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-upload-pack.adoc:48
#, no-wrap
msgid "<directory>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-upload-pack.adoc:50
msgid "The repository to sync from."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-upload-pack.adoc:52
#, no-wrap
msgid "ENVIRONMENT"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-upload-pack.adoc:54
#, no-wrap
msgid "`GIT_PROTOCOL`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-upload-pack.adoc:58
msgid ""
"Internal variable used for handshaking the wire protocol. Server admins may "
"need to configure some transports to allow this variable to be passed. See "
"the discussion in linkgit:git[1]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-upload-pack.adoc:59
#, no-wrap
msgid "`GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-upload-pack.adoc:68
msgid ""
"When cloning or fetching from a partial repository (i.e., one itself cloned "
"with `--filter`), the server-side `upload-pack` may need to fetch extra "
"objects from its upstream in order to complete the request. By default, "
"`upload-pack` will refuse to perform such a lazy fetch, because `git fetch` "
"may run arbitrary commands specified in configuration and hooks of the "
"source repository (and `upload-pack` tries to be safe to run even in "
"untrusted `.git` directories)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-upload-pack.adoc:74
msgid ""
"This is implemented by having `upload-pack` internally set the "
"`GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH` variable to `1`. If you want to override it (because you "
"are fetching from a partial clone, and you are sure you trust it), you can "
"explicitly set `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH` to `0`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-upload-pack.adoc:76
#, no-wrap
msgid "SECURITY"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-upload-pack.adoc:83
msgid ""
"Most Git commands should not be run in an untrusted `.git` directory (see "
"the section `SECURITY` in linkgit:git[1]). `upload-pack` tries to avoid any "
"dangerous configuration options or hooks from the repository it's serving, "
"making it safe to clone an untrusted directory and run commands on the "
"resulting clone."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-upload-pack.adoc:87
msgid ""
"For an extra level of safety, you may be able to run `upload-pack` as an "
"alternate user. The details will be platform dependent, but on many systems "
"you can run:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-upload-pack.adoc:89
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    git clone --no-local --upload-pack='sudo -u nobody git-upload-pack' "
"...\n"
msgstr ""

